.TH EUCLID-CLI-EAP-LIST-NODES 1 "October 2026" "euclid-cli 1.0.53" "Euclid CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
euclid-cli-eap-list-nodes \- list the registered worker nodes
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B euclid-cli eap list-nodes
.SH DESCRIPTION
Lists the worker nodes registered in the caller's account \- the hosts
running
.B euclid-wrk
that euclid places applications on. For each node:
.TP
.I name
What the node calls itself, and what assignments are written against.
.TP
.I address
The IP address the worker reported: the one it reaches the master from,
unless it was configured otherwise.
.TP
.IR os ", " arch
The operating system and CPU architecture the worker was built for, e.g.
\fIlinux\fR and \fIaarch64\fR. Placement matches them as the labels
\fIos\fR and \fIarch\fR, and they cannot be overridden by configuration.
.TP
.I labels
The labels from the worker's configuration that an application's
\fInodeLabels\fR are matched against.
.TP
.IR cpuCount ", " version
How many CPUs the node has, and the euclid version the worker is built
from.
.TP
.I drained
Whether the node has been taken out of placement. A drained node keeps
running what it has.
.TP
.IR live ", " lastSeen
Whether the node has renewed recently enough to be given work, and when
it last did.
.TP
.I principal
The principal that registered the node, and the only one allowed to
renew it.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The nodes are printed as JSON.
.TP
.B 1
The caller is not an authenticated administrator, or the request failed.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli eap list-nodes
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR euclid-cli-eap (1),
.BR euclid-wrk (8),
